40            *** USER PROCESSING AND SETTINGS ***
41            ************************************
42             1) REQUIRED - PhUSE CS Utilities macro library.
43                These templates require the PhUSE CS macro utilities:
44                  https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/utilities
45                User must ensure that SAS can find PhUSE CS macros in the SASAUTOS path (see EXECUTE ONE TIME, below)
46             2) OPTIONAL - Subset measurement data, to limit resulting plots to specific
47                  - Parameters
48                  - Analysis Timepoints
49                  - Visits
50             3) REQUIRED - Key user settings (libraries, data sets, variables and box plot options)
51                M_LB:   Libname containing ADaM measurement data, such as ADVS.
52                        WORK by default, since step (2) creates the desired WORK subset.
53                M_DS:   Measuments data set, such as ADVS.
                                                           The SAS System

54                T_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Name, such as TRTP, TRTA.
55                TN_VAR: Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Number (display controls order), such as TRTPN, TRTAN.
56                M_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with measurements data, such as AVAL.
57                C_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with change-from-baseline data, such as CHG.
58                LO_VAR: Variable in M_DS with LOWER LIMIT of reference range, such as ANRLO.
59                        Required to highlight values outside reference range (RED DOT in box plot), and reference lines
60                HI_VAR: Variable in M_DS with UPPER LIMIT of reference range, such as ANRHI.
61                        Required to highlight values outside reference range (RED DOT in box plot), and reference lines
62                B_VAR:    (Leave blank to omit p-value from summary table.) Variable in M_DS with baseline measurements
63                REF_TRTN: (Leave blank to omit p-value from summary table.) Numeric value of TN_VAR for reference (comparator)
63       ! treatment
64                B_VISN: Visit number that represents Baseline in AVISITN (e.g., 0)
65                E_VISN: Visit number that represents endpoint in AVISITN for chg-from-baseline comparison (e.g., 99)
66                        OPTIONAL: Include additional visits BETWEEN baseline and endpoint.
67                                  List space-delimited, INCREASING visit numbers in E_VISN.
68                                  The LAST (greatest) visit number in E_VISN is the endpoint visit.
69                P_FL:  Population flag variable. 'Y' indicates record is in population of interest.
70                A_FL:  Analysis Flag variable.   'Y' indicates that record is selected for analysis.
71                REF_LINES:
72                      Option to specify which Normal Range reference lines to include in box plots
73                      <NONE | UNIFORM | NARROW | ALL | numeric-value(s)> See discussion in Central Tendency White Paper
74                      NONE    - No reference lines on box plot
75                      UNIFORM - Preferred alternative to default. Only plot LOW/HIGH ref lines if they are uniform for all
75       ! measurements
76                      NARROW  - Default. Display only the narrow normal limits: max LOW, and min HIGH limits
77                      ALL     - Discouraged, since displaying ALL reference lines confuses review of data display
78                      numeric-values - space-delimited list of reference line values, such as a 0 reference line for displays of
78       ! change.
79                MAX_BOXES_PER_PAGE:
80                      Maximum number of boxes to display per plot page (see "Notes", above)
81                OUTPUTS_FOLDER:
82                      Location to write PDF outputs (WITHOUT final back- or forward-slash)
