3              Display:     Figure 7.8 Box plot - Last/Min/Max Baseline versus Post-baseline Measurements by Treatment and Analysis
3        ! Timepoint, Multiple Studies
4              White paper: Central Tendency
5          
6              User Guide:     https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/blob/master/whitepapers/CentralTendency-UserGuide.txt
7              Macro Library:  https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/utilities
8              Specs:          https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/specification
9              Test Data:      https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/data/adam/cdisc-split
10             Sample Output:  https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/blob/master/whitepapers/WPCT/outputs_sas/WPCT-F.07.08_ ...
10       !  _timepoint_815.pdf
11         
12             Using this program:
13         
14               * Figure 7.8 is intended Integrated Summaries involving a large number of studies. In such cases, displaying
14       ! by-study results
15                 becomes unreasonable. Instead, pool studies and report Last, Min and Max Baseline vs. Last, Min and Max
15       ! Post-baseline measures.
16         
17               * See USER PROCESSING AND SETTINGS, below, to configure this program for your environment and data
18               * Program will plot all visits, ordered by AVISITN, with maximum of 20 boxes on a page (default)
19                 + see user option MAX_BOXES_PER_PAGE, below, to change limit of 20 boxes per page
20               * Program separately plots all parameters provided in PARAMCD
21               * Measurements within each PARAMCD and ATPTN determine precision of statistical results
22                 + MEAN gets 1 extra decimal, STD DEV gets 2 extra decimals
23                 + see macro UTIL_VALUE_FORMAT to modify this behavior
24               * If your treatment names are too long for the summary table, abbreviate them
25                 in the input data, and add a footnote that explains your short Tx codes
26                 + This program contains custom code to shorted Tx labels in the PhUSE CS test data
27                 + See "2b) USER SUBSET of data", below
28         
29             TO DO list for program:
30         
31               * Reduce the title/footnotes font size, to match Fig. 7.1 and Fig. 7.2 (or increase those to match this Fig. 7.3)
32         
33               * Complete and confirm specifications (see Outliers & Reference limit discussions, below)
34                   https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/specification
35               * The footnote could dynamically describe any normal range lines that appear. See the Fig. 7.1 specifications.
36               * For annotated RED CIRCLEs outside normal range limits
37                   UPDATE the test data so that default outputs have some IQR OUTLIER SQUAREs that are not also RED.
38               * LABS & ECG - ADaM VS/LAB/ECG domains have some different variables and variable naming conventions.
39                   - What variables are used for LAB/ECG box plots?
40                   - What visits/time-points are relevant to LAB/ECG box plots?
41                   - Handle all of these within one template program?
42                     Or separate them (and accept some redundancy)?
43                   - NB: Currently vars like AVISIT, AVISITN, ATPT, ATPTN are hard-coded in this program CS: attempted to remove
43       ! hardcode of these variables.
44         
45         end HEADER ***/
